  1: # S01 Theme: the Astryx "lane" theme
  2: 
  3: Version 1.0.0, 2026-10-30. Depends on: S00, DESIGN.md sections 3 to 6 and 11. Blocks: S04, S05 to S08.
  4: 
  5: ## 1. Purpose
  6: 
  7: Turn the Astryx substrate into this site's theme so every Astryx component the chrome uses (Button, Link, Kbd, Toast, BottomSheet) draws in the site's blue, type and motion, and none of it reads as Meta's stock UI. The theme is built with the CLI, committed, and drift-checked.
  8: 
  9: ## 2. What was verified before this spec was written
 10: 
 11: On 2026-10-30, in a scratch project with `@astryxdesign/core@0.7.1` and `@astryxdesign/cli@0.7.1`, the mapping in DESIGN.md section 11 was written as `defineTheme` and built with `astryx theme build ... --json`. Result: `tokenCount 84`, `sizeKB 11.3`, `warnings []`, one notice that the font is named but not loaded (handled by S00 fonts.css). Resolved values were read back from the CSS: durations 100/150/225/200/300/450ms, `--ease-standard` as configured, font sizes 13/16/20/25/31/39/49/61px, radii 2/4/6/14px. So the API shape in section 4 is known to work; the builder is not guessing.
 12: 
 13: ## 3. Steps
 14: 
 15: 1. `npx astryx init --features theme` in the repo root. This writes `theme.template.ts` (reference only; do not import it) and agent docs. Commit the agent docs; read them.
 16: 2. Run and save to `qa/astryx/` (these are receipts and the source of legal override keys):
 17:    - `npx astryx theme targets Button --json > qa/astryx/targets-button.json`
 18:    - same for `Kbd`, `Toast`, `BottomSheet`, `Link`
 19:    - `npx astryx component BottomSheet --dense > qa/astryx/BottomSheet.txt` (and for Button, Link, Kbd, Toast)
 20:    - `npx astryx doctor --json > qa/astryx/doctor.json`
 21: 3. Write `themes/lane/laneTheme.mjs` exactly as section 4, reading values from `tokens.generated.json` (no literal colors in the theme file).
 22: 4. For each entry in section 5, confirm the key exists in the saved targets JSON. If a key is not listed, do not invent one: use the documented data-attribute escape hatch (`astryx docs styling/styling-advanced`) inside `@layer jp-chrome`, and record the substitution in this spec's changelog.
 23: 5. `npm run theme`, then `npm run theme:check`. Commit `themes/lane/dist/*`.
 24: 6. Write `src/styles/global.css` regime block (section 6).
 25: 
 26: ## 4. Theme source
 27: 
 28: ```js
 29: // themes/lane/laneTheme.mjs
 30: import {defineTheme} from '@astryxdesign/core/theme';
 31: import T from './tokens.generated.json' with {type: 'json'};
 32: 
 33: const c = T.color;
 34: const mono = {family: 'Commit Mono', fallbacks: '"Commit Mono Fallback", ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace'};
 35: 
 36: export const laneTheme = defineTheme({
 37:   name: 'lane',
 38:   typography: {scale: T.type.scale, body: mono, heading: mono, code: mono},
 39:   radius: {base: T.radius.base, multiplier: T.radius.multiplier},
 40:   motion: {...T.motion.astryxMotion, easing: T.motion.easePlain},
 41:   tokens: {
 42:     '--color-accent': [c.paper.accent, c.void.accent],
 43:     '--color-on-accent': [c.paper.ground, c.void.ground],
 44:     '--color-text-accent': [c.paper.accent, c.void.accent],
 45:     '--color-icon-accent': [c.paper.accent, c.void.accent],
 46:     '--color-accent-muted': [c.accentMutedLight, c.accentMutedDark],
 47:     '--color-background-body': [c.paper.ground, c.void.ground],
 48:     '--color-background-surface': [c.paper.raised, c.void.raised],
 49:     '--color-background-card': [c.paper.raised, c.void.raised],
 50:     '--color-background-popover': [c.paper.raised, c.void.raised],
 51:     '--color-text-primary': [c.paper.text, c.void.text],
 52:     '--color-text-secondary': [c.paper.text2, c.void.text2],
 53:     '--color-icon-primary': [c.paper.text, c.void.text],
 54:     '--color-icon-secondary': [c.paper.text2, c.void.text2],
 55:     '--color-border': [c.paper.hairline, c.void.hairline],
 56:     '--color-error': [c.errorLight, c.errorDark],
 57:     '--focus-outline-color': [c.paper.accent, c.void.accent],
 58:     '--shadow-low': 'none',
 59:     '--shadow-med': 'none',
 60:     '--shadow-high': 'none',
 61:     '--size-element-sm': `${T.size.elementPx.sm}px`,
 62:     '--size-element-md': `${T.size.elementPx.md}px`,
 63:     '--size-element-lg': `${T.size.elementPx.lg}px`,
 64:   },
 65:   adaptations: {
 66:     rules: [
