 83: 
 84: Never shown, by rule: GPA (brief line 10; cut by Justin 2026-10-04), phone, model names Ollama serves, any metric, any liveness claim about the server or the projects.
 85: 
 86: Conflict resolved: the brief calls LeafLink mutual aid and earlier notes called it event discovery. Justin confirmed mutual aid on 2026-10-30 (D-LEAFLINK-KIND).
 87: 
 88: ## 6. Reframes taken
 89: 
 90: - **"Seamless travel between scenes" became "one object that re-forms", not a camera flight.** Flying a camera between three separate places is the 3D-portfolio default. Here there is one field of lanes and travel changes its layout weights; the camera only settles. That is why the three scenes read as one site.
 91: - **"Blue accent" became "blue owned by lightness and job".** The measurement in DESIGN 3.1 showed no saturated mid blue is ownable, and Astryx ships Meta's. So signal is only light on dark and ink is only marks on paper; neither is ever a brand-band button fill.
 92: - **"Bold" became one structural decision instead of many effects.** One draw call, three light regimes, one typeface, zero ornaments.
 93: - **The hero became the server itself.** The brief's strongest fact is that he runs his own inference on hardware he owns. The geometry is that hardware's core count, so the picture is a claim, not decoration.
 94: 
 95: ## 7. Counter-cases, stated fairly
 96: 
 97: - **"This is a particle hero."** The ban list kills decorative dot fields "even when the dots are data-driven". The defense: the lanes are not behind a headline, they are the scene's only drawing; on LeafLink they are the streets the matches travel, on SideQuests the plan and the trails. If a blind reviewer still reads the Server scene as ambient decoration (G-ANTI question 2, "matrix rain screensaver"), that is K-SRV-3 and the scene is redesigned, not defended.
 98: - **Density saturation.** At the first-guess alpha the 6,144 lanes fused into a solid block. The tuned values fixed it on desktop and phone renders in SwiftShader, but a real phone at DPR 3 draws thinner lines with different blending. G-PERF-DEVICE screenshots are the check; alpha is a token, so the fix is one number.
 99: - **700ms travel versus "nothing over 250ms".** Travel is longer than the feedback budget. DESIGN 6.2 reconciles it: the key press lights within one frame, the readout swaps by 150ms, 80% of the displacement happens in the first 210ms, and travel is interruptible. If testers still feel the wait, the duration token drops; the choreography table is written in fractions so it scales.
100: - **Monospace type reads "developer portfolio".** Commit Mono is the common choice for that genre. It is kept because the navigation is a terminal and the person is a systems engineer; the defense is that it is the only typeface and it is used at display size weight 200, which the genre rarely does. A reviewer naming the type as the generic part would be a fair hit.
101: - **"Live map" on a simulated feed.** C-LL-P1 describes what LeafLink is (the brief's words), while the scene runs a simulation. C-LL-SIM says "Simulated feed" on the same screen so nobody reads the drawing as live data.
102: 
103: ## 8. Changelog
104: 
105: - 1.0.0, 2026-10-30: initial run on the package.
106: - 1.0.1, 2026-10-30: Justin's rulings on R-GPU, D-SQ-VENUE and D-LEAFLINK-KIND recorded.
