 1: # Style Brief: Portfolio (v2)
 2: Source: design-extract on corentinbernadou.com (Awwwards SOTD Mar 25 2026) and bruno-simon.com (Awwwards SOTD Jan 21 2026); both portfolio genre, three.js + GSAP.
 3: Date: 2026-10-04. Raw artifacts: `~/workspace/portfolio/design-extract/`.
 4: 
 5: ## Design language
 6: Dark editorial instrument panel. Near-black warm canvas, one hot accent, flat material, hairline structure, tight Swiss typography. Restraint is the luxury: 7 total unique colors detected on the reference; nothing decorative survives without a job.
 7: 
 8: ## Tokens
 9: ```css
10: :root {
11:   --bg-0: #070304;        /* page canvas (warm near-black) */
12:   --bg-1: #141414;        /* raised surfaces */
13:   --ink-0: #f5f5f5;       /* primary text */
14:   --ink-1: #858585;       /* secondary text */
15:   --ink-2: #575757;       /* tertiary / captions */
16:   --accent: #ff4401;      /* PLACEHOLDER: reference brand color, do not ship as-is */
17:   --accent-deep: #980000;
18:   --line: #1f1f1f;        /* hairline rules */
19:   --radius: 3px;          /* max radius anywhere */
20:   --space-base: 2px;
21:   --ease-out: cubic-bezier(0.25, 0.46, 0.45, 0.94);
22:   --dur-md: 300ms;
23: }
24: ```
25: Accent judgment call (flagged): the reference ships red `#ff0000` as brand. Justin's site needs its own signal color. Proposal: signal amber `#ffb000` (instrumentation/lab connotation, fits "engineer who verifies"; AA on near-black at large sizes, check body sizes). Alternative: keep the red-orange family. Claude/Justin to lock.
26: 
27: ## Typography
28: - Headings: tight, Title Case, semibold. Narrow measure for prose (~38-60ch).
29: - Type ladder (from bruno-simon, measured at true 1x; ratio ~1.25 major third from 16px): display 64 / title-1 50 / h2 40 / title-2 34 / title-3 30 / body 20 / body-sm 16 / micro 13 (bold). Line-height tight on headings (1.05-1.15), body 1.5-1.6.
30: - Body: neutral grotesk (embedded open-licensed equivalent; no proprietary font files). Display accent: one expressive face for the hero thesis line only (reference uses a handwritten display face; Justin's pick is a judgment call, must stay terse-compatible).
31: - Micro labels: uppercase, letterspaced, tertiary ink (section eyebrows, captions, receipts).
32: 
33: ## Spacing and layout
34: - 2px base increments; section rhythm generous (reference: 21px vertical unit at its scale; translate to 8pt-ish rhythm at real scale).
35: - Narrow editorial content column for prose; full-bleed for dossier rows and the hero scene.
36: - 12-column grid discipline; hairline rules (`--line`) separate sections instead of cards.
37: 
38: ## Material
39: - Flat. No shadows, no gradients, no glassmorphism, no backdrop blur. Radius 3px max on UI chrome (reference range 3-8px; media may go to 8px, never pill-shaped).
40: - Depth comes from the 3D scene and from layering ink tones, not from elevation tokens.
41: - Note: bruno-simon color tokens were noisy (extractor caught a loading state; 100% white dominance). Color system stays on the Bernadou-derived dark canvas; do not lift Bruno's red.
42: 
43: ## Motion (from motion tokens)
44: - 300ms ease-out `cubic-bezier(0.25, 0.46, 0.45, 0.94)` for UI feedback; "responsive" feel.
45: - Scroll-linked choreography for the hero rig and timeline (GSAP ScrollTrigger scrub).
46: - Matches the spec §8 budgets (welcome <1.4s, transitions 220ms).
47: 
48: ## Stealable patterns
49: 1. Hairline-ruled editorial sections with micro-label eyebrows.
50: 2. Narrow prose measure with full-bleed media breaks.
51: 3. Scroll-linked 3D geometry behind flat editorial content (depth without decoration).
52: 4. Persistent micro-labels as wayfinding (section numbers, receipt tags).
53: 
54: ## Anti-patterns to avoid (from this reference)
55: - Do not lift the red brand color or the issue-numbering editorial system ("Issue N°003") — that is Bernadou's identity.
56: - Do not copy the grid-ruler interaction or the cursor mask nav — signature interactions, not patterns.
57: - The reference's fixed tiny type scale is a zoom artifact; do not reproduce absolute px values.
58: 
59: ## Do-not-copy list
60: Logos, brand marks, photography, the red `#ff0000` brand color, issue-numbering system, grid-ruler tool, cursor-mask nav, proprietary fonts. Substitute: open-licensed grotesk, Justin's own accent, original 3D rig.
</file>

<file path="src/chrome/CopyConfirm.ts">
 1: // CopyConfirm (S04 section 7.3): the copy result toast, through
 2: // Astryx useToast with stock anatomy and token colors. This hook
 3: // encapsulates the copy plus toast behavior so ContactSheet stays a
 4: // pure layout component. On copy failure the address text node is
 5: // selected with a Range so the user can copy manually.
 6: import { useToast } from '@astryxdesign/core';
 7: import { C } from '../copy';
 8: import { copyText } from '../lib/copyText';
 9: 
10: export interface CopyConfirm {
11:   copyEmail: (email: string, addressEl: HTMLElement | null) => Promise<void>;
12: }
13: 
14: export function useCopyConfirm(): CopyConfirm {
15:   const showToast = useToast();
16:   async function copyEmail(email: string, addressEl: HTMLElement | null): Promise<void> {
17:     const ok = await copyText(email);
18:     if (ok) {
19:       showToast({ body: C['C-TOAST-OK'], type: 'info', uniqueID: 'copy' });
20:       return;
21:     }
22:     if (addressEl) {
23:       const range = document.createRange();
24:       range.selectNodeContents(addressEl);
25:       const selection = window.getSelection();
26:       if (selection) {
27:         selection.removeAllRanges();
28:         selection.addRange(range);
29:       }
30:     }
31:     showToast({ body: C['C-TOAST-FAIL'], type: 'error', uniqueID: 'copy' });
32:   }
33:   return { copyEmail };
