  1: # S07 Scene: SideQuests, community engagement (`/sidequests`)
  2: 
  3: Version 1.1.0, 2026-11-01. Depends on: S02, S03, S04, S09, DESIGN `world.sidequests`, `world.camera.sidequests`, `motion.spring`. Blocks: S10 poster, S11 scene gates.
  4: 
  5: ## 1. Purpose
  6: 
  7: SideQuests turned a campus into a place people show up to. This scene is a chalk plan of a campus on blueprint blue, built from the same 6,144 lanes: a faint grid, building outlines with hatching, curved walkways, and three dashed quest trails leading from a trailhead to three markers. Tap a marker and its trail lights up dash by dash from the trailhead, the camera leans along with it, and the marker plants itself. It is the playful scene: the one place on the site where things overshoot.
  8: 
  9: ## 2. Visual identity
 10: 
 11: - Ground: field `#10294E`, the accent family used as the ground (the only scene where hue is the field). Chalk `#F5F1E9` for lines, chalk 2 for secondary, signal blue only on lit trails and claimed markers (under 6% of pixels).
 12: - Vocabulary: architectural plan, not a game map. Grid at 10%, outlines at 85%, 45-degree hatching at 22%, walkways at 45%, trails as dashes at 55%, lit trails at 100% with a signal rim.
 13: - Motion: spring and wander. Markers bob on slow sines with different phases; a claimed marker drops into place with one overshoot (damping ratio 0.7); trails are curves, never straight.
 14: - Not a game HUD: no score, no XP, no badges, no progress bar, no quest names (the real quests are UNKNOWN), no completion message.
 15: 
 16: ## 3. Layout
 17: 
 18: ### 3.1 Plan generator (`src/world/layouts/sidequests.ts`, worker)
 19: 
 20: Use `rng(seed + 2 * 1000003)`. Plane `y = 0`, extent 36 by 28 centered at the origin (`x in [-18, 18]`, `z in [-14, 14]`).
 21: 
 22: 1. **Grid (2,080 lanes, class 4).** Vertical lines at `x = -18, -17, ..., 18` (37 lines), each split into 28 lanes of length 1 along z. Horizontal lines at `z = -14, ..., 14` (29 lines), each split into 36 lanes of length 1 along x. `37 * 28 + 29 * 36 = 2080`.
 23: 2. **Buildings (11).** Rejection-sample axis-aligned footprints inside `x in [-16, 16]`, `z in [-12, 10]` (the strip `z > 10` stays open for the trailhead). Width and depth uniform in `[2.0, 6.5]`. With probability 0.35 the footprint is an L: remove one corner rectangle whose sides are 30% to 50% of the footprint's sides. Bounding boxes keep `minGap` 1.2 apart. Up to 500 attempts; if fewer than 11 fit, restart the whole step with `rng(seed + 2 * 1000003 + attempt)`. Each building gets one entrance at the midpoint of its edge that faces the most open space (largest distance to the nearest other footprint along the edge normal).
 24: 3. **Outlines (class 5).** Each footprint edge of length `L` is split into `max(1, round(L / 0.5))` straight lanes.
 25: 4. **Walkways (class 7).** Build the minimum spanning tree over the 11 entrances (Euclidean). Keep its 9 shortest edges. Each walkway is a centripetal Catmull-Rom through: entrance A, `lerp(A, B, 0.33) + n * o1`, `lerp(A, B, 0.66) + n * o2`, entrance B, where `n` is the unit normal of AB and `o1, o2 = (r() * 0.15 + 0.15) * |AB| * (r() < 0.5 ? -1 : 1)`. If sampled points fall inside any footprint, flip the offset signs; if still inside, use a straight line. Split by arc length into lanes of about 0.4 units (`count = max(1, round(arcLength / 0.4))`); each lane's 8 points are sampled along its arc interval, so walkway lanes are curved.
 26: 5. **Markers (3) and trails (class 8).** Trailhead `start = (0, 0, 13)`. Candidate marker points: every integer grid point in the building region that is at least 0.8 from any footprint and at least 8 from the start. Pick 3 by seeded farthest-point sampling (first pick random, then the candidate maximizing the minimum distance to picks so far), requiring at least 9 units between markers. Each trail is a centripetal Catmull-Rom through `start`, three waypoints at `lerp(start, marker, f) + perp * (r() * 2 - 1) * 3` for `f = 0.25, 0.5, 0.75` (nudged 0.8 out of any footprint they land in), and the marker. Cut by arc length into dashes: dash 0.3, gap 0.2; each dash is one lane with 8 points on its arc. Keep each trail's lane ids in order from start to marker.
 27: 6. **Hatch (class 6), the remainder.** `N = 6144 - (2080 + outlines + walkways + trails)`; assert `N > 0`. Inside each footprint polygon, generate 45-degree lines at spacing 0.35, clip to the polygon, giving segments. If the segment count exceeds `N`, multiply spacing by 1.1 and retry. Allocate exactly `N` lanes across segments by length with the S06 step 5 algorithm (quota, `max(1, floor)`, distribute remainder, trim excess). Assert the grand total is 6,144.
 28: 7. **Side data:** marker positions, the three trails' ordered lane id lists with per-lane arc start and length, footprints (for tests).
 29: 
 30: Expected counts with the default seed (record actuals in the build state file): outlines about 400, walkways about 600, trails about 180, hatch about 2,880.
 31: 
 32: ### 3.2 Camera and framing
 33: 
 34: Fine: camera `(6, 24, 16)` looking at the origin, fov 36, shift `-0.18` NDC in x (the plan sits left, the trailhead readout right). Coarse: `(3, 30, 14)`, fov 46, shift `-0.22` in y (plan lower, readout top). Idle yaw `±2 deg` over 30s.
 35: 
 36: The plan view is not a state of the scene.
 37: 
 38: **Camera band (W1, DESIGN.md section 6.6).** The SideQuests camera pitch stays inside `world.sidequests.camera.pitchMin` -75 to `world.sidequests.camera.pitchMax` -5 in every frame, including init, restore, morph, walk, resize, and reduced motion. The band scope is every frame, not the fully active scene only: the band is wide enough to admit morph transit (shallowest legitimate morph frame -10.97 coarse server endpoint, -10.22 fine server endpoint derived from token poses; steepest legitimate frame -69.62 walk lean; flat -90). Yaw gets no band: it wraps through plus and minus 180 during morphs and is not the axis that produces the flat read. The plan layout (grid, outline, hatch, walkway, trail lanes) stays ambient structure, seen only through the scene's normal camera, never presented flat from above. The clamp sits at the single final write point in W4; where it engages during a walk, the walk still finishes its trail.
 39: 
 40: **Readability rule:** only grid lanes (class 4, 10% alpha) may appear behind the readout box. T-SQ-3 checks the worst-case text contrast against the actual pixels.
 41: 
 42: ### 3.3 Markers (`src/world/sidequests.ts`)
 43: 
 44: Three markers, one `InstancedMesh` for heads and one for poles (2 draw calls). Head: `OctahedronGeometry(0.35)` scaled y by 1.4, flat two-tone with no lighting: vertex colors chalk on the upper four faces, chalk 2 on the lower four (`MeshBasicMaterial({vertexColors: true})`). Pole: `CylinderGeometry(0.02, 0.02, 0.8, 6)` in chalk 2. The head sits on top of the pole, `y` from 0.8 plus bob. Claimed: head color uniform switches both tones to signal and signal dim.
 45: 
 46: **DOM twins are the hit targets.** Three `<button>`s (Astryx `Button variant="ghost" isIconOnly`, `label` C-SQ-MARKER, `aria-pressed` reflects claimed) absolutely positioned over each marker's projected head position every frame (`transform: translate(x, y)` only), 44 by 44 CSS px, transparent, focus ring visible on `:focus-visible`. No canvas hit testing is needed in this scene.
 47: 
 48: ### 3.4 Readout (variant `sidequests`, the trailhead sign)
 49: 
 50: C-SQ-H1 (display-1), C-SQ-P1, C-SQ-FACTS, C-SQ-VENUE, C-SQ-CODE (link), C-SQ-HINT (pointer-appropriate variant). Dashed chalk outline per S04. World region `aria-label` C-SQ-ALT.
 51: 
 52: ### 3.5 Hero mark (W1)
 53: 
 54: The SideQuests hero is the project's brand mark, rendered by `BrandHero` (DESIGN.md sections 3.5, 6.8, 9) at the hero anchor inside the scene. Descriptor: kind mark, ring r, mark sidequests. The shipped mark is `sidequests.gif` from opensourcery/sidequests (branch dev, app/assets/sidequests.gif); `sidequests-alpha.gif` is DO NOT USE and never ships. The hero holds exactly one mark: no second image shares the viewport.
 55: 
 56: Placement: outside the name clear zone (`zone.name.padPx`), outside the readout clear zone (the trailhead sign), and outside the keymap. Displayed size comes from `hero.sizePx` and `hero.minSizePx`, fitted inside the brand area cap (`brand.areaCap` 0.12 at 390x844) from the mark's aspect ratio; the cap governs. Gradient: `scene.sidequests.gradient` (lead field, tail signal, tailLength 0.8, wander light that follows the wander path; overshoot moments brighten). Passive motion: drift along the wander path, settling with the existing spring, continuous. Active motion: pointer or touch-drag tilts the plane within `hero.tiltMaxDeg` 8; a tap sends one ripple through the ring (150ms out, 700ms settle). Under reduced motion the hero shows the static PNG with an identity transform. The hero rectangle never overlaps any marker tap target (the three 44 by 44 CSS px twins), so a tap on the logo (ripple) and a tap on a marker (walk) can never conflict (T-HERO-3).
 57: 
 58: ## 4. Motion
 59: 
 60: | Phase | What | Duration, easing, trigger |
 61: |---|---|---|
 62: | Entry (travel in) | Lanes loosen into the plan; ground to field (plain ease); camera to the plan pose. Markers rise from `y = 0` to rest with the spring (staggered 80ms apart) after travel resolves. | 700ms expo-out; spring 0.7 / 3.2Hz |
 63: | Hero (morph in) | The deflection ring grows at the hero anchor during Gather; the mark looms in during Reveal (DESIGN.md section 6.7). On exit the mark recedes and the ring collapses. | Inside travel 700ms |
 64: | Hero (idle and active) | Passive wander drift with spring settle, continuous. Tilt on pointer or touch-drag within 8 degrees; tap ripple through the ring. | Ripple 150ms out, 700ms settle |
 65: | Idle | Marker bob `0.06 * sin(2 pi t / 2.4 + phase_i)`, phases `0, 2.1, 4.2` rad. Camera yaw. | Sine, linear time |
 66: | Hover (fine pointer) | Hovered twin: marker head lifts 0.15 units by spring; cursor pointer. Leaving returns it by spring. | Spring |
 67: | Walk (tap, click, Enter or Space on a twin) | `setActivity(trailLanes, start_i = now + arcStart_i / 14, fadeAt 0, kind 2, uPerSec = 14 / laneLength_i)`; the first dash lights on the next frame. Camera target damps toward the current drawing point with weight 0.25 (half-life 400ms) while drawing, then back to the pose. | 14 units per second; first feedback under one frame |
 68: | Claim (trail fully drawn) | Marker head color to signal over `--duration-fast` ease; head drops from `y + 0.6` to rest by spring (one overshoot, about 4.6% of 0.6 below rest). `aria-pressed=true`. | Spring |
 69: | Re-walk a claimed marker | Clear that trail's activity and walk again. | As walk |
 70: | Exit | Controller pauses; trails stay lit (state is kept for the visit); markers sink to `y = 0` with `uW.z`. | With travel |
 71: | Reduced motion | No bob, no yaw, no hover lift. Walk lights the whole trail at once (`uPerSec` very large) and claims instantly; colors switch without transition. | Static |
 72: 
 73: Claimed state lives in memory for the visit only. Nothing is stored.
 74: 
 75: ## 5. Content
 76: 
 77: S09 IDs: C-TITLE-SIDEQUESTS, C-SQ-H1, C-SQ-P1, C-SQ-FACTS, C-SQ-VENUE, C-SQ-CODE, C-SQ-HINT, C-SQ-MARKER, C-SQ-ALT. No text in the scene.
 78: 
 79: ## 6. Components
 80: 
 81: | Thing | Start from | Notes |
 82: |---|---|---|
 83: | Plan lanes | S02 Lanefield | layout `sidequests` |
 84: | Markers | three.js `InstancedMesh`, `OctahedronGeometry`, `CylinderGeometry`, `MeshBasicMaterial` | no lights in the scene |
 85: | Marker twins | Astryx `Button variant="ghost" isIconOnly` | the visual is the 3D marker; the button is the target and the focus ring |
 86: | Readout | S04 `Readout variant="sidequests"` | |
 87: 
 88: ## 7. Kill criteria
 89: 
 90: - K-SQ-1: any score, badge, XP, progress bar, quest name, or "you did it" message.
 91: - K-SQ-2: overshoot anywhere other than marker position (never on color, opacity, or the camera).
 92: - K-SQ-3: any trail is straight or any two trails overlap for more than 2 units.
 93: - K-SQ-4: a marker can only be operated by pointer (twins missing or unfocusable).
 94: - K-SQ-5: anything but grid lanes behind the readout.
 95: - K-SQ-6: signal pixels over 6% with all three trails lit.
 96: 
 97: ## 8. Receipts
 98: 
 99: | Test | Claim | How |
100: |---|---|---|
101: | T-SQ-1 | Exact allocation | worker unit test: grid 2,080, total 6,144, hatch N matches, 11 buildings, 3 markers at least 9 apart |
102: | T-SQ-2 | Walk feedback | Playwright clicks twin 1; on the next rAF the trail's first lane has `start <= now()`; after `length / 14 + 0.2` s, `aria-pressed="true"` |
103: | T-SQ-3 | Readout contrast | screenshot; for each text line box, compute contrast of the text color against the lightest pixel behind it (render once with readout hidden): at least 4.5 |
104: | T-SQ-4 | Spring numbers | sample marker head y during claim: minimum is between 0.020 and 0.035 below rest, settles within 0.005 by 0.6s |
