132: ## 3. Item 3: mobile intuitiveness plus camera tracking
133: 
134: ### 3.1 The symbolic link, stated once
135: 
136: The image must show what the message says, in the visitor's own hands:
137: 
138: - **LeafLink** (leaflink-readme.md): mutual aid on a map. An offer meets a need, nothing central watches. The image: the visitor drops an offer, a route draws to a request, and when it lands, a pulse travels from that spot on the map into the LeafLink mark. The thing they did ends inside the mark.
139: - **SideQuests**: decentralized, self-hostable quests. The image: the visitor picks a trail, the camera brings that trail's marker into view beside the mark (where a clear pan exists, 10.2), the trail draws to it, and the claim lands with one beat on the sign. The quest they walked ends next to the sign, never under it.
140: 
141: ### 3.2 Repro
142: 
143: | Symptom | Root cause | Measured |
144: |---|---|---|
145: | LeafLink verb not reachable on a phone | `scenes/leaflink.tsx:65`: the facts block sits before the offer button, so at 390x658 the button is below the 46dvh slip (`chrome.css:322`). | button 571..603 vs slip bottom 598: hidden |
146: | SideQuests walk happens off screen | Markers sit under the readout or off screen at phone aspect; S07 lean (`sidequests.ts:284` `followPoint.set(start…)`) snaps toward the trailhead and the pitch clamp then pins it. | pitch -64.49 to -75 in one frame; marker never in the clear band |
147: | Claim fires early | `sidequests.ts:129` `walkLength` sums dash lengths only; `layouts/sidequests.ts:943` advances `s += dash + gap`. | claim at 60% of the arc |
148: | No visible verb on SideQuests (coarse) | Twins are the only controls and they are invisible tap targets on markers. | 0 visible controls |
149: | Mark beats on a timer | `heroGeometry.ts:175` `heroBeatScaleAt` is periodic, contradicting DESIGN 6.3 (LeafLink is event driven). | periodic beat |
150: 
151: ### 3.3 Decisions
152: 
153: 1. **Stage grammar** (`src/motion/stage.ts`, DESIGN 6.12): controllers emit `subject`, `land`, `beat`, `release`; BrandHero is the only listener that moves the camera or the mark. One owner each.
154: 2. **Coarse-only focus pan.** On coarse viewports (`useCoarse`: width under 768, or coarse pointer under 1024), `subject` pans the camera so the subject (the destination: the LeafLink request node, the SideQuests trail's marker) sits at a focus spot just above or below the mark (`focusSpotsFor`): its center one 44px coarse target plus `hero.ringPadPx` plus the mark's motion margin from the mark edge, clear of the readout, name zone, and keymap. Only a spot whose straight pan never sweeps the subject under the mark counts (`pathCrossesMark`); of those, the nearest (`nearestSpot`); with none, no pan. The pan is a ground translation of position and target: pitch never changes, the SideQuests band [-75, -5] is untouched, ITEM 6 clamp stays the last write. Damped with `focus.halfLifeMs` 200, capped at `focus.maxPanWorld` 20. Fine viewports never pan (the whole map is in view) and keep the S07 lean.
155: 3. **Hold, do not chase.** The pan holds the destination at its spot for the whole walk, so the drawing head travels toward a marker already in view. The first version followed the drawing head with a look-ahead; that swept the marker across the mark mid-walk and failed T-HERO-BAND-WALK, so the `track` event and the look-ahead were removed.
156: 4. **Tap on the mark is the page verb.** LeafLink: drop an offer at the map center. SideQuests: walk the next open trail. A half-strength pulse from the tap point gives feedback in the same frame.
157: 5. **Event beats.** `heroBeatEnvelope(msSinceBeat, amp)` replaces the periodic beat. Any LeafLink match landing beats at `hero.beatScale` 1.015; the visitor's own match lands at `hero.landBeatScale` 1.04.
158: 6. **LeafLink order.** H1, P1, legend, SIM, OfferButton, rule, facts, stack, code. The verb comes before the reference material.
159: 7. **SideQuests coarse trail row.** Three visible Astryx ghost `sm` buttons "Trail 1/2/3" in the plate (`.jp-sq-trail`, dashed bar glyph, `aria-pressed` when claimed). On coarse the twins become pointer-only (`aria-hidden`, `tabIndex -1`); on fine they stay the accessible controls.
160: 8. **Reduced motion.** No pan, no recede, no pulse. The verb still works and the claim still lands.
