237: ## 5. Item 5: stochastic shapeshifter motion
238: 
239: ### 5.1 Decision
240: 
241: Motion varies per visit and per page; layout never does. One 32-bit session seed drives every random motion choice. Draws are counter based, so a value depends only on the seed and the draw count of its channel, never on frame timing. That is what makes it testable: same seed plus same input sequence gives the same frames.
242: 
243: ### 5.2 Entropy source (`src/motion/entropy.ts`)
244: 
245: ```ts
246: // splitmix32 finalizer over (seed, channel, index). Pure and total.
247: export function hash32(s: number, channel: number, index: number): number {
248:   let z = (s ^ Math.imul(channel, 0x9e3779b9) ^ Math.imul(index + 1, 0x85ebca6b)) >>> 0;
249:   z = Math.imul(z ^ (z >>> 16), 0x21f0aaad) >>> 0;
250:   z = Math.imul(z ^ (z >>> 15), 0x735a2d97) >>> 0;
251:   return (z ^ (z >>> 15)) >>> 0;
252: }
253: export function drawAt(s: number, channel: EntropyChannel, index: number): number {
254:   return hash32(s, CHANNEL_ID[channel], index) / 4294967296;
255: }
256: ```
257: 
258: - Seed: `?seed=<uint32>` (token `entropy.seedParam`), else one `crypto.getRandomValues` value. Read once at app boot (`App.tsx` module scope calls `entropySeed()`), because the first draw happens inside travel, after the router's `pushState` has already replaced the URL without its query. `Math.random` is not used for motion.
259: - Found by T-ENT-REPLAY, not by the pure suite: reading the seed lazily at first draw silently fell back to a random seed, so two `?seed=1234` loads gave bow -0.642 and -1.131 on the same first morph. The pure tests call `resetEntropy(seed)` directly and could not see it. After the fix both loads draw bow -0.330 from seed 1234.
260: - Channels: `morph-bow`, `morph-swirl`, `morph-pull`, `pulse-swirl`, `glitter-swirl`, each with its own counter.
261: - `world.seed` (layout hash, LeafLink sim sequence, T-LL-2) is separate and never changes.
262: - Debug: `window.__entropy = { seed, enabled, counters }`.
263: 
264: ### 5.3 Parameter ranges and per-page variation
265: 
266: | Parameter | Range | Where it acts |
267: |---|---|---|
268: | Camera bow | signed, up to `entropy.scene.<to>.bowWorld` | lateral ground translation times sin(pi times eased progress): zero at both ends, rides the camera's own curve, pitch invariant |
269: | Ring swirl | signed, up to `entropy.scene.<to>.swirl` | tangential share of the ring push, same C1 falloff |
270: | Pull scale | `entropy.pullScale` [0.85, 1.15] | multiplier on `morph.silhouettePull` |
271: | Pulse swirl | signed, up to `entropy.pulseSwirl` 0.6 | taps and land pulses |
272: | Glitter swirl | signed, up to `glitter.swirl` 0.9 | GLITTERBOX hold |
273: 
274: | Destination | bowWorld | swirl | Why |
275: |---|---|---|---|
276: | server | 0 | 0 | Lockstep: the server arrives rigid, every time |
277: | leaflink | 1.5 | 0.35 | moderate, organic |
278: | sidequests | 2.5 | 0.7 | widest, wandering |
279: | scatter | 2.0 | 0.9 | glitter only |
280: 
281: Keyed by destination, so each page keeps its signature (DESIGN 6.3) while no two visits are identical.
282: 
283: ### 5.4 Perf budget
284: 
285: Cost is one float uniform (`uRingSwirl`), one two-float ground offset added to an existing camera write, and five hashes per morph (not per frame, not per lane). No new draw call, no new texture, no per-lane CPU work. The vertex shader adds one multiply-add on the existing deflection term. p95 16.7ms holds by construction; device run 3 measures it (section 8.3), and if it does not hold, the fix is a DESIGN.md patch with the measurement, never a quiet lowering.
286: 
287: ### 5.5 Reduced motion
288: 
289: Deterministic: `setEntropyEnabled(false)` makes `unit()` return 0.5 and `signed()` return 0, so bow 0, swirl 0, pull scale 1, identical for every seed. `+ 0` folds the negative zero a signed draw times a zero range produces.
290: 
291: ### 5.6 Stochastic verification
292: 
293: | Test | Asserts |
294: |---|---|
295: | T-ENT-1 (pure) | same seed reproduces: a fixed 24-navigation script cycling all destinations gives `toEqual` (bow, swirl, pull scale) arrays |
296: | T-ENT-2 (pure) | different seeds vary: more than half the script's values differ between seed 1 and seed 2 (server bow and swirl are rigid by token, so only its pull scale varies) |
297: | T-ENT-3 (pure) | reduced motion is neutral and seed independent: seeds 7 and 99999 give identical arrays of exactly bow 0, swirl 0, pull scale 1 |
298: | T-ENT-4 (pure) | ranges for 2,000 seeds: every draw inside its token range, server bow and swirl exactly 0 (`toBe(0)`, so no negative zero), `drawAt` in [0, 1) |
299: | T-ENT-5 (pure) | for 200 seeds and every from/to pair, the bow factor is 0 at p 0 and at p 1 and the ring strength is 0 at travel end |
300: | T-ENT-REPLAY (browser) | the full script 2, 3, 1 sampled every 16ms (bow, swirl, ring strength, pan) is `toEqual` for seed 1234 twice and `not.toEqual` for seed 98765 |
301: | AGY seed sweep (section 9) | 512 seeds: replay identical, distribution in range, frame budget per seed |
302: 
303: **The clock has to be paused.** T-ENT-REPLAY's next failure was the harness, not the product: `page.clock.install` alone keeps page time flowing with wall time, so under load a step was sometimes 32ms instead of 16ms (sampled p 0.1243 then 0.17 in one run, 0.1471 in the other). The tests and both trace scripts now call `page.clock.pauseAt` after load, so `runFor` is the only clock, and the first input is put on the 16ms frame grid. With that, two seed-1234 loads match to the last digit (ring strength 0.4046 on the same frame in both). The round-2 receipts were taken before the pause: their geometry is exact, their ms stamps are good to about one frame.
304: 
305: **What "same seed reproduces" means, precisely.** Same seed, same input script, same viewport, same loaded state. The last term matters: the hero anchor, and so the Gather start, resolves on the first frame after the brand manifest has arrived (a ring never renders at an unresolved anchor). The manifest is real network I/O, so a replay that starts sampling before it arrives can differ in ring strength by a frame or two of Gather while bow and swirl stay identical. T-ENT-REPLAY's first run showed exactly that (ring strength 0 vs 0.400 on the third sampled frame, bow and swirl equal), so the test now waits for `window.__brandPrefetched` before the script starts. This is a test precondition, not a product change: on a cold first visit the mark simply places a little later, once, at its final position.
