439: ### 10.2 Open decision for Justin: phone camera pan vs T-HERO-BAND-WALK
440: 
441: The existing gate T-HERO-BAND-WALK says the mark never overlaps a marker during a walk. It is right, and it holds. It also limits item 3 on phones. The pan moves the whole plan in a straight line, and for some trails every straight pan that would bring the marker into view crosses the mark on the way. Those trails now get no pan. Measured: at 390x844, trail 2 pans into view beside the mark and trails 1 and 3 stay where they are. At 390x658 (Justin's in-app browser) there is no spot beside the mark at all (above is the readout, below is the keymap), so no SideQuests trail pans. That viewport behaves as before this round. The LeafLink verb, the readout order, the trail row, and the land beat are unaffected.
