517: +
518: +One 32-bit session seed drives every random motion choice: `?seed=<uint32>` (token `entropy.seedParam`) replays a run exactly; otherwise one value from `crypto.getRandomValues`. The seed is read once at app boot, before the router's first `pushState` drops the query. Draws are counter based: draw(channel, n) is a pure hash of (seed, channel, n) (splitmix32 finalizer), so a value depends only on the seed and how many draws that channel has made, never on frame timing. Channels: morph bow, morph swirl, morph pull, pulse swirl, glitter swirl. `Math.random` is not used for motion. The layout seed `world.seed` is separate and never changes (layout hash, LeafLink sim sequence, T-LL-2 stay fixed).
