583: // ---- T-HERO-UV: mask UV orientation is not mirrored. The mounted
584: // hero is the DOM image, upright; the mask is the same image drawn
585: // letterboxed into a square canvas and uploaded with flipY false,
586: // and the shader maps u with world x and v with world z. This test
587: // pins the three facts the orientation claim rests on: the source
588: // mapping grows v with z, the upload sets flipY false, and the
589: // camera projection puts larger world z lower on screen (so v
590: // growing with z is screen-down, the same direction as image rows
591: // growing downward). If any of those flipped, the bunching would
592: // mirror: the SideQuests mark is strongly asymmetric vertically
593: // (row quartile 2 holds 95268 opaque pixels against 17061 in
594: // quartile 0), so a flip would move the bunching mass visibly.
