 12: //
 13: // What changed in polish round 2, each tied to a device-run-2 repro:
 14: //
 15: // 1. Placement is computed once per page configuration, synchronously,
 16: //    in a layout effect at mount (the readout swap commit). Travel now
 17: //    conceals the readout with visibility plus inert instead of the
 18: //    hidden attribute, so the readout rect exists at this point, and
 19: //    the brand manifest is read from the shared cache, so no network
 20: //    turn sits between mount and placement. There is no per-frame
 21: //    re-track: the old re-track placed against a hidden readout
 22: //    (LeafLink: logo centered at 198,326 for 225ms, then a 160px jump
 23: //    to 262,166 when the readout returned) and chased moving marker
 24: //    projections during the morph. SideQuests marker blockers come from
 25: //    the resting projection (lanefield.projectAtRest), which does not
 26: //    move with the camera, so the placement is the same in every frame.
 27: //    Placement re-runs only on viewport resize.
 28: // 2. The placed center is registered as the lane field hero anchor, so
 29: //    the morph ring, the silhouette pull, and every pulse sit under the
 30: //    logo on screen (the old ring sat at the camera target: 103px left
 31: //    and 88px below the LeafLink logo, 124px above the SideQuests logo
 32: //    inside the readout). The ring radius is clamped to the clearance
