 351: ## 9. Imagery and assets
 352: 
 353: No photos, no illustrations, no icons except Astryx's built-in external-link indicator on `Link isExternalLink`. No logos of Ollama, Docker, Tailscale, NVIDIA or anyone else: product names appear as text only. No map tiles, no real street data, no Leaflet marker graphic. Every visual is procedural from S02, S05, S06, S07.
 354: 
 355: **Brand-marks exception (the only logos on the site).** The two project marks ship as real GIF assets from Codeberg, pinned by commit SHA and recorded with sha256 in a manifest (W3 owns the pipeline). SideQuests hero: `sidequests.gif` from opensourcery/sidequests (branch dev, app/assets/sidequests.gif), 1920x538, 4 frames, 42591 bytes. LeafLink hero: W3 confirms whether `leaves.gif` (bon3head/LeafLink, branch main, app/assets/leaves.gif, 305x400, 50 frames, 828040 bytes) or `logo.png` (same repo, public/logo.png, 1024x1024 RGBA, 174622 bytes) is the shipped mark; `logo.png` is also the reduced-motion PNG and the F1 fallback source for LeafLink. `sidequests-alpha.gif` is DO NOT USE: it adds the word "alpha" below the logo and stays reference only. The hero holds exactly one mark per project route. Feedback-05 and feedback-08 are not placed on any page this round; circuit.gif and gears.gif are creative liberty only, never heroes.
 356: 
 357: **Delivery markup (per project hero).** A `picture` element: a `source` for reduced motion pointing at the first-frame PNG, and an `img` pointing at the GIF with the approved alt text, explicit width and height, `decoding="async"`, and `data-brand-mark` set to the project. The first-frame PNG is extracted from the GIF at build time and is identical to GIF frame 0. The PNG renders first, at Reveal. The GIF loads behind it and replaces it on `img.decode()` resolve, with no fade, since an identical frame means no visible onset. A script listener on reduced motion forces the PNG at runtime even if `picture` does not re-evaluate.
 358: 
 359: **Fallback chain (each level is tested).** F0: the GIF decodes and its natural size matches the manifest, so the animated GIF shows. F1: network or decode error, size mismatch with the manifest (truncated file), or not decoded within `brand.decodeTimeoutMs` 4000 (proposed), with no retry loop, so the first-frame PNG shows, static. F2: the PNG also fails, so a text mark shows: the approved alt text's project name in Commit Mono 700, signal color, sentence case, centered in the ring. Lanes still deflect, so the hero still exists. F3: WebGL unavailable (the existing field fallback), so the F0, F1, or F2 image shows without deflection, over the flat field.
 360: 
 361: **Build-time checks.** Frame count, loop duration, per-frame delays, dimensions, transparency flag, edge fringe (near-white pixels next to transparent ones), the union of all frame palettes (the hue fingerprint), and byte size. If the GIF is matted against white, W3 re-mattes its edge pixels per frame against transparency; T-ASSET-4 must pass on the navy field, or W3 stops.
 362: 
 363: **Budgets (proposed).** 900 KB transferred per GIF (token `brand.gifMaxBytes` 900000) and decoded memory (width times height times 4 times frames) of 48 MB or less (token `brand.gifMaxDecoded` 48000000). If over budget, first run lossless `gifsicle -O3`, then resize to displayed size times 3 DPR, keeping the same GIF and the same animation. If still over budget, stop and report. Switching format away from GIF needs Justin's yes, because he asked for the actual GIFs. W0 measured budgets: sidequests.gif 42591 bytes transferred and 16527360 bytes decoded (15.8 MB); leaves.gif 828040 bytes transferred and 24400000 bytes decoded (23.3 MB); both inside budget.
 364: 
 365: **Alt text rule.** Alt text is the project name plus what the mark depicts, 12 words or fewer, never starting with the words "image of". The final alt strings are drafted in W0 section 6 and finalized by W3; W1 writes only this rule. W0 drafts, recorded here as drafts and not as final copy: "SideQuests logo, green handwritten wordmark with a star"; "LeafLink logo, animated green maple leaf"; "LeafLink logo, green leaves forming a smile". The same string drives the F2 text mark, so the alt text physically appears in the theme when the image fails. No other copy changes in this round.
 366: 
 367: ## 10. What this system never does
 368: 
 369: Gradients in chrome. Glow without a source. Glass or blur. Drop shadows. Cards, nested or not. Eyebrows. All caps. Stat grids. Counters of fake activity. "Live" or "online" indicators of any kind. Decorative particle fields (every drawn element is a lane, a pulse, a pin, a marker or a word, and each encodes something). Cursor trails. Scroll-jacking. Bounce on color or opacity. Orthogonal-routed lines, pads, silkscreen labels or designators (the PCB direction is dead and the lane field must never read as a circuit board: lanes are parallel, flat streets, or curves; they never turn 90 degrees in a routed pattern in the Server scene).
