1088: - 1.7.0, 2026-11-10: server words formed from lanes (section 6.15, S05 1.3.0), Justin's pick for fix 4b of the guestbook phone brief over removing them, since C-SRV-P2 no longer carries the stack names. Each character rides its own lane tip; bend and tint follow the word's opacity so lanes never snap. Word lanes reuse the guestbook offset texture (alpha 2 plus slot) with one tint per `wordPool` slot; lane draw calls unchanged; no new tokens, no copy change.
1089: - 1.6.0, 2026-11-10: guestbook on real phones (Justin's iPhone demo, Safari and an in-app browser). Section 6.14 gains phone frame, keyboard, contrast and scene-word rules; tokens `guestbook.dim.*` (amount 0.94, pad 24px, feather 64px) and `guestbook.focusRulePx` 2 are new and proposed until a device run confirms them. Contrast is the lane-dim option because G-TOKENS bans gradients in CSS (a CSS radial scrim would fail the lint). The projection now reads the canvas's CSS box, which was `100dvh` tall while the camera aspect used `innerHeight`. Uniforms nine to twelve; draw calls unchanged. Lock-in choreography unchanged.
1090: - 1.5.0, 2026-11-09: guestbook (section 6.14, `guestbook.*` new). Brief: `guestbook/prompt.md` on astryx-polish-r2 (entropic and 3D). Two Lusion beziers enter as guestbook-only curves (`guestbook.easeMain`, `guestbook.easeSoft`, from `guestbook/references/lusion-style-brief.md`); the site curves are unchanged. Pill radius 88 from the same extract. Engine adds one RGBA32F 256 by 24 texture (98,304 bytes) and nine uniforms; draw calls unchanged. Proposed values: every `guestbook.*` number is proposed until a device run confirms it. Storage: browser-local only (Justin, 2026-11-10); a shared store, if ever wanted, is a separate change.
